1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,256
Orchard Core is a content management system and application framework built on ASP.NET Core.

2
00:00:07,256 --> 00:00:11,533
A dotnet new template creates a web application that uses it.

3
00:00:11,533 --> 00:00:16,321
In this video, we install the template, create a project, run it, set

4
00:00:16,321 --> 00:00:18,300
up the site, and sign in.

5
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:29,496
An Orchard Core site is an ASP.NET Core web application that references the Orchard Core packages.

6
00:00:29,496 --> 00:00:31,525
You can build one by hand:

7
00:00:31,525 --> 00:00:36,599
create an empty web project, add the CMS package, register Orchard Core in

8
00:00:36,599 --> 00:00:39,580
Program.cs, and remove the default pages.

9
00:00:40,330 --> 00:00:43,018
The template does that work in one command.

10
00:00:43,018 --> 00:00:47,241
It writes the project file, the logging setup, and the launch settings.

11
00:00:47,241 --> 00:00:51,300
By default, the package versions match the version of the templates.

12
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:58,249
You need the .NET SDK and a terminal.

13
00:00:58,249 --> 00:01:02,851
The templates are one NuGet package, OrchardCore.ProjectTemplates.

14
00:01:02,851 --> 00:01:07,070
Install it once, with dotnet new install and the package ID.

15
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:12,045
To install a specific release, add an at sign and the version number

16
00:01:12,045 --> 00:01:13,587
after the package ID.

17
00:01:13,587 --> 00:01:18,840
Preview packages come from a separate NuGet source, which the documentation describes.

18
00:01:19,590 --> 00:01:26,030
The package also holds templates for an MVC web application, for modules, and for themes.

19
00:01:26,030 --> 00:01:27,928
Each has a short name.

20
00:01:27,928 --> 00:01:31,250
The one for a CMS web application is occms.

21
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:39,692
Create an empty folder, open a terminal in it, and run dotnet new

22
00:01:39,692 --> 00:01:41,664
occms with the name option.

23
00:01:41,664 --> 00:01:45,428
The name becomes the project folder and the project file.

24
00:01:45,428 --> 00:01:47,280
Here, the name is MySite.

25
00:01:48,030 --> 00:01:53,202
The folder holds the project file, Program.cs, an app settings file, the NLog

26
00:01:53,202 --> 00:01:56,006
configuration, and the launch settings.

27
00:01:56,006 --> 00:02:00,680
Orchard Core itself comes from NuGet packages, not from source files.

28
00:02:01,430 --> 00:02:04,447
The project file references two packages.

29
00:02:04,447 --> 00:02:06,822
One provides logging with NLog.

30
00:02:06,822 --> 00:02:13,240
The other, the CMS targets package, brings in the Orchard Core modules and the starter themes.

31
00:02:13,990 --> 00:02:18,840
The CMS targets package builds on a smaller one, the CMS Core targets package:

32
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:22,536
the modules and the admin theme, without front end themes.

33
00:02:22,536 --> 00:02:27,790
The documentation suggests it for headless sites, and for sites with their own theme.

34
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:31,522
Program.cs has three Orchard Core lines.

35
00:02:31,522 --> 00:02:34,180
Use N Log Host connects the logger.

36
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:39,625
Add Orchard CMS registers the services, and Use Orchard Core adds Orchard Core

37
00:02:39,625 --> 00:02:41,570
to the request pipeline.

38
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:44,441
The template takes options.

39
00:02:44,441 --> 00:02:48,876
Logger selects NLog, Serilog, or none, and NLog is the default.

40
00:02:48,876 --> 00:02:52,604
Orchard Version selects the version of the packages.

41
00:02:52,604 --> 00:02:56,460
Framework selects the target framework of the project.

42
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:04,754
Run the application with dotnet run, and pass the path of the project

43
00:03:04,754 --> 00:03:06,664
file with the project option.

44
00:03:06,664 --> 00:03:09,230
Run it from the folder that holds MySite.

45
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:15,153
The MySite profile in the launch settings defines two addresses:

46
00:03:15,153 --> 00:03:18,700
https on port 5001, and http on port 5000.

47
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:22,616
The console prints both when the server starts.

48
00:03:22,616 --> 00:03:25,720
Open the https address in a browser.

49
00:03:29,931 --> 00:03:34,497
The site is not set up yet, so the first request shows the Setup screen.

50
00:03:34,497 --> 00:03:39,121
It asks a few questions about the site, its database, and its super user.

51
00:03:39,582 --> 00:03:41,052
Let's name the site.

52
00:03:41,052 --> 00:03:44,332
The name is used as the default title of your pages.

53
00:03:44,784 --> 00:03:49,450
Recipes set up a site with pre-configured options, features and settings.

54
00:03:49,450 --> 00:03:53,466
The Recipe menu lists the ones that come with the CMS package.

55
00:03:53,466 --> 00:03:54,884
Let's choose Blog.

56
00:03:55,334 --> 00:03:59,086
Default Time Zone is the time zone used by default when dates and

57
00:03:59,086 --> 00:04:01,042
times are displayed and edited.

58
00:04:01,042 --> 00:04:02,944
Choose the one your site uses.

59
00:04:03,399 --> 00:04:07,198
The database is Sqlite, which needs no connection string.

60
00:04:07,198 --> 00:04:11,419
It stores the data of the site in a file in the App_Data folder.

61
00:04:11,871 --> 00:04:14,275
The super user has all the rights.

62
00:04:14,275 --> 00:04:19,685
Let's enter a user name, an email address, and a password, and confirm the password.

63
00:04:19,685 --> 00:04:23,531
The Password field shows the rules a password must follow.

64
00:04:23,993 --> 00:04:25,562
Select Finish Setup.

65
00:04:25,562 --> 00:04:29,603
A few seconds later, Orchard Core redirects to the home page.

66
00:04:29,603 --> 00:04:33,403
The Blog recipe created this blog, and the site is ready.

67
00:04:37,611 --> 00:04:39,742
The admin site is at /admin.

68
00:04:39,742 --> 00:04:44,191
You are not signed in yet, so Orchard Core shows the Log in page.

69
00:04:44,644 --> 00:04:49,424
Enter the user name of the super user and its password, and select Log in.

70
00:04:50,346 --> 00:04:52,717
The admin opens with a welcome message:

71
00:04:52,717 --> 00:04:54,034
your site is ready.

72
00:04:54,034 --> 00:04:58,196
Browse the menu to see what you can configure, and start writing content.

73
00:05:02,396 --> 00:05:06,794
The NLog configuration sends the logs to a file in the logs folder

74
00:05:06,794 --> 00:05:09,298
of App_Data, one file for each day.

75
00:05:09,298 --> 00:05:14,856
The hosting lifetime events, such as the listening addresses, also go to the console.

76
00:05:15,606 --> 00:05:19,623
The log levels come from the Logging section of the app settings file.

77
00:05:19,623 --> 00:05:22,636
Change the Default level there to log more or less.

78
00:05:23,386 --> 00:05:28,753
With the Serilog option, the template adds the Serilog package, a Serilog section

79
00:05:28,753 --> 00:05:32,331
in the app settings file, and no NLog configuration.

80
00:05:32,331 --> 00:05:35,046
With none, it adds no logging package.

81
00:05:35,796 --> 00:05:38,408
App_Data holds the data of the site:

82
00:05:38,408 --> 00:05:42,202
the Sqlite database file, uploaded media, and the logs.

83
00:05:42,202 --> 00:05:47,986
The ORCHARD_APP_DATA environment variable sets another folder for the data of the site.

84
00:05:48,736 --> 00:05:52,413
To stop the server, press Control and C in the terminal.

85
00:05:52,413 --> 00:05:57,396
The data stays in App_Data, so running the project again starts the same site.

86
00:06:01,596 --> 00:06:05,378
The same package has templates for modules and themes:

87
00:06:05,378 --> 00:06:07,268
ocmodulecms and octheme.

88
00:06:07,268 --> 00:06:13,256
Create them next to the web application, and reference them from it, to extend your site.

89
00:06:14,006 --> 00:06:19,720
To install a site without the Setup screen, add the Auto Setup feature to Program.cs.

90
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:24,806
It sets the site up on the first request, from values in the configuration.

91
00:06:26,806 --> 00:06:30,180
That is a running Orchard Core site from one template:

92
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:33,724
install it once, create a project, run it, and set it up.

93
00:06:33,724 --> 00:06:35,186
Thanks for watching.

